text.section:
The Director may administer and enforce the provisions of this chapter. In administering and enforcing the provisions of this chapter pursuant to the findings and legislative policy adopted by the General Assembly, the Director shall exercise the following powers in addition to any other powers conferred upon him by law:

Supervise the administration and enforcement of this chapter and all regulations and orders adopted thereunder;


Issue orders to enforce the provisions of this chapter, all regulations adopted thereunder, and the terms and conditions of any permit;


Make investigations and inspections to ensure compliance with any provision of this chapter or any regulation or order adopted thereunder;


Encourage and conduct investigations, research, experiments, and demonstrations and collect and disseminate information relating to surface mining and reclamation of lands and waters affected by surface mining; and


Receive any federal funds, state funds, or any other funds and enter into any contracts for which funds are available to carry out the purposes of this chapter.
